      "content": "It sounds like you are in deep pain, and it makes complete sense that your identity feels shattered when someone you care about has suffered deeply. Please know that self-hatred is often a symptom of carrying a profound burden, not proof that you are unworthy, and many people remind themselves they are victims of circumstances just as much as they are responsible for their actions. I hope you can find a compassionate psychologist who specializes in trauma to help you explore the depth of your emotions and begin the very difficult process of reclaiming your sense of self.",
